## HIT list (3 HIT classes, dispositions printed)
- **HIT-OV (peak overlap > peakOverlapMaxPct 40) ×3 peak events** (purpose · this · Goddamnit): measured overflow into a neighbour's base ink exceeds the Plan's 40% bound, concentrated on narrow neighbours ("in" = 8.8 px ink — any centred growth >3.5 px/side breaches it) and on the shout pair. DISPOSITION — carried into the wave printed: the overlap is the technique's OBSERVED form (census frames + the Execute motion montage show purpose/this glyphs crossing both neighbours and Goddamnit crossing into "Gump!" while it stays white and legible at its onset edge); the peaked word paints above neighbours (z-index while env>0) exactly as the film's peak glyph occludes. The 40% figure was a Plan estimate, not a source measurement; the ratios themselves are specimen-true and do not move (Plan failure point 1: "the ratio is the source's"). Neighbour words remain fully rendered beneath; no neighbour is reflowed or wrapped (reserved slots).
- **HIT-FLOOR (guard check 3 reading):** base-state ink height measures 7.75–8.25 px at the 360 stage, below the guard's ~11 px ink-height floor, while the Plan's own binding floor — `minBasePxAt360` = 11 px FONT size — passes (11.34 ≥ 11). DISPOSITION — carried printed: the two floors are different quantities (font px vs glyph ink height; Liberation Bold cap height ≈0.73 em). Every PEAK state (the technique subject) measures 11.00–16.50 px ink height, above the floor; base words are the pre-light/supporting state. Raising base size further would depart from the amended Plan's priced 5.6% (plan-review finding 5's cure) — not done unilaterally.
- **Weight evidence limit (not a HIT, a printed limit):** this seat carries only static Liberation faces (Regular/Bold); Roboto Flex is not installed, so intermediate `wght` values cannot be rendered/measured here — the continuous-weight claim prints **UNVERIFIED on this stack** (Plan's priced risk, construction section). The build sets `font-variation-settings 'wght'` from CONFIG every frame; on a variable-font stack the axis is live.


